\section{Introduction}
Faifi (Faifa, Fayfi; ISO 639-3 fif; Glottocode faif1234) is spoken around the Fifa mountains of Jizan province, southwestern Saudi Arabia. Its status is debated: some treat it as an unusual Arabic dialect, others as a possible descendant of Ancient South Arabian. Wikipedia gives about 50,000 speakers; younger speakers are shifting to other varieties.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Faifi language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faifi_language}
\item Alfaifi et al. 2025 (paper on Faifi): \url{https://faculty.ksu.edu.sa/sites/default/files/Alfaifi_etal_2025.pdf}
\item Thesis, Aspects of the morphosyntax of the Faifa dialect of Saudi Arabic (Ulster): \url{https://pure.ulster.ac.uk/en/studentTheses/aspects-of-the-morphosyntax-of-the-faifa-dialect-of-saudi-arabic-/}
\item Benjamins catalogue entry: \url{https://lwc1.benjamins.com/catalog/sal.11.05alf}
\item Leeds talk, preliminary observations on Faifi Arabic emphatic fricatives: \url{https://www.latl.leeds.ac.uk/events/some-preliminary-observations-on-a-variety-of-faifi-arabic-with-a-focus-on-emphatic-fricatives/}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project, Faifi in Saudi Arabia: \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/21997/SA}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The available material is academic description of the variety; no teaching materials or school programmes were found. Schooling in the area uses Standard Arabic, and Faifi has no known written standard.

